ases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 26, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a doctor and nurse about different types of melanoma.\n\nWhich type of maligna is commonly found on the nail beds?\n\nA. Superficial Spreading melanoma\n\nB. Acral-Lentiginous melanoma\n\nC. Lentigo Maligna", "sourcePage": 136, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 27, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a doctor and nurse about lung cancer.\n\nThe lung cancer that originates in the surrounding membrane of the lungs is;\n\nA. Mesothelioma carcinoma\n\nB. Large cell carcinoma\n\nC. Squamous cell carcinoma", "sourcePage": 137, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 28, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a doctor and nurse about non-inflamed comedones.\n\nWhich of the following types of comedones is also called milia?\n\nA. Soft closed comedones\n\nB. Hard closed comedones\n\nC. Microcomedones", "sourcePage": 137, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 29, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a doctor and nurse about Acnes.\n\nWhich of the following types of acne occurs only on face?\n\nA. Acne Cosmetica\n\nB. Acne Rosacea\n\nC. Acne vulgaris", "sourcePage": 137, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 30, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a doctor and nurse about Athlete’s foot.\n\nAthlete’s foot caused by Trichophyton mentagrophytes is;\n\nA. Chronic Scaly Athlete’s Foot\n\nB. Chronic Interdigital Athlete’s Foot\n\nC. Acute Vesicular Athlete’s Foot\n\n                                            Part C\nIn this part of the test, you'll hear two different extracts. In each extract, you'll hear health\nprofessionals talking about specific aspects of their work.\n\nFor questions, 31 to 42 choose the answer (A, B, or C) which fits best according to what you\nhear. Complete the answers as you listen the audio.\n\nNow, look at extract one.", "sourcePage": 138, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["e284ff5b129a15384a32740e1cb398a369f2526e078205f38479eba2501404db"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [144]}], "matchEvidence": "Reviewed patient cases and question topics in the exact-recording transcript against the printed task paper; task filename alone is not used", "notice": "The recording calls the patient Delilah; the printed case says Garcia/Gracia. The case details and subsequent extracts match. Original wording is retained."}, {"id": "british-academy-task-12-C", "label": "British Academy · Task 12 · Part C", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "pages": [139, 140, 141, 142, 143], "questions": [{"number": 31, "prompt": "Which type of ADD patients are called space cadets?\n\nA. Inattentive Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nB. Classic Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nC. Overfocused Attention Deficit Disorder", "sourcePage": 139, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 32, "prompt": "Patient with type 2 ADD will have\n\nA. Decreased blood flow in their brain area of prefrontal cortex, cerebellum and basal ganglia.\n\nB. Deficiency of dopamine and serotonin\n\nC. Reduced activity in the prefrontal cortex as well as low levels of dopamine.", "sourcePage": 139, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 33, "prompt": "Which of the following conditions is more common in girls than boys?\n\nA. Overfocused Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nB. Inattentive Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nC. Temporal Lobe Attention Deficit Disorder", "sourcePage": 140, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 34, "prompt": "In which of the following conditions, the treatment is aimed to soothe neuronal activity\n& stop nerve cells from over-firing or firing unpredictably.\n\nA. Temporal Lobe Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nB. Overfocused Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nC. Ring of Fire Attention Deficit Disorder", "sourcePage": 140, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 35, "prompt": "Patients might see or hear things that are not there in;\n\nA. Anxious Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nB. Ring of Fire Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nC. Temporal Lobe Attention Deficit Disorder", "sourcePage": 140, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 36, "prompt": "Patients will have an overactive brain in;\n\nA. Overfocused Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nB. Ring of Fire Attention Deficit Disorder\n\nC. Anxious Attention Deficit Disorder", "sourcePage": 141, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 37, "prompt": "Which of the following statements suits best with this extract?\n\nA. Most of the scleroderma affect the internal organs.\n\nB. Scleroderma is a symptom of a complicated group of diseases.\n\nC. Systemic sclerosis affects only certain parts of the body.", "sourcePage": 141, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 38, "prompt": "The characteristics of a linear scleroderma is;\n\nA. Abnormally colored skin\n\nB. Reddish oval-shaped patches\n\nC. The centers of the patches appear ivory, with violet borders", "sourcePage": 141, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 39, "prompt": "Small blood vessels of hands or feet contract in response to cold or anxiety in;\n\nA. Telangiectasias syndrome\n\nB. Raynaud's phenomenon\n\nC. Sclerodactyly syndrome", "sourcePage": 142, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 40, "prompt": "In which of the following syndromes, small red spots on the hands and face caused by\nswelling of tiny blood vessels?\n\nA. Raynaud's phenomenon\n\nB. Sclerodactyly syndrome\n\nC. Telangiectasias syndrome", "sourcePage": 142, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 41, "prompt": "Raynaud's phenomenon is experienced for years before skin thickening becomes\nevident in;\n\nA. Limited scleroderma\n\nB. Diffuse scleroderma\n\nC. Linear scleroderma", "sourcePage": 142, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 42, "prompt": "Less collagen is produced during the phase called ‘softening’ in;\n\nA. Linear scleroderma\n\nB. Diffuse scleroderma\n\nC. Limited scleroderma", "sourcePage": 143, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 144, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["e284ff5b129a15384a32740e1cb398a369f2526e078205f38479eba2501404db"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e